=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ HISTSH @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt HISTSH @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-histsh): DCL command history across sessions, early test
1 'NOTICE
=prompt HISTSH is distributed under the MIT licence. This is an early test release.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [HISTSH]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for HISTSH (vms-histsh)
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:HISTSH$STARTUP.COM
    At login, add as the LAST line of SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGIN.COM:
    $ IF F$SEARCH("HISTSH:HISTSH_START.COM") .NES. "" THEN @HISTSH:HISTSH_START
    For each user, with AUTHORIZE (ADD/IDENTIFIER once):
    UAF> ADD/IDENTIFIER HISTSH$USER
    UAF> GRANT/IDENTIFIER HISTSH$USER username

PRODUCT REMOVE HISTSH deassigns HISTSH$ROOT and HISTSH; users' history files
are kept. Take the SYLOGIN line out first, or it just finds nothing to run.
